/-!
# A073932

Define f(n) = n - largest nontrivial divisor of n or f(n) = n-1 if n is a prime [that is, f(n) = A060681(n)]. Form a triangle in which the n-th row contains terms n, f(n), f(f(n)), ... until a 1 is reached; sequence gives triangle read by rows.

The 95 terms known to OEIS, indexed from `1`.

Skeleton generated by `lake exe oeis-gen`; every declaration is a `sorry` placeholder.
-/

